# Difference Between Subquery and Join

| Subquery | Join |
|----------|------|
|Query inside another query|Combines multiple tables|
|Can be nested|Usually faster|
|Easy to understand|Better performance for large datasets|
|May execute multiple times|Executed once by optimizer|

---

# Advantages

- Easy to write
- Easy to understand
- Reduces complex SQL
- Useful with Aggregate Functions
- Useful for filtering

---

# Disadvantages

- Can be slower than joins
- Difficult to debug
- Correlated subqueries may be expensive

